      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A randomly chosen population in the area of Westphalia (West Germany) was screened for apolipoprotein A-I mutants. About 5000 individuals were investigated and compared with a group of 1300 patients who had undergone coronary angiography. Four electrophoretically different apolipoprotein A-I-mutants (named Münster-1 to 4) were discovered. Five non-related probands were observed in the group of the unselected patients and three non-related probands in the group of coronary angiography patients. In most cases the familial nature of the abnormality was confirmed by pedigree analysis."},
